@3051 = ~Defender of Amn~

@3052 = ~Defender of Amn was once presented to one of the fairest soldiers in Amnian service, a young guardian whose determination to drive out crime was surpassed only by his faith in the goodness of others. He hoped to make his country a safer, kinder place.

That faith became his undoing. A band of orcs approached the gates of Athkatla professing peaceful intentions. Trusting their word, the soldier allowed them through without collecting the required toll. Once inside, the orcs pillaged several buildings and murdered an innocent citizen before escaping.

Dismissed from service and shunned by those who had praised him, the soldier found himself consumed by guilt. Unable to bear the disgrace or forgive himself, he took his own life. His shield passed into his family's keeping, a gilded reminder that even honourable intentions may have tragic consequences.

STATISTICS:

Armor Class Bonus: +3
Armor Class Bonus vs. Missile Attacks: +5 (total)~

@3053 = ~Brewer's Draught of Disinterest~

@3054 = ~An unusual golden draught sealed with a sapphire-blue stopper. The brewer claims it can diminish a man's romantic appetites. Larissa asked for this potion as part of a desperate attempt to salvage her marriage. It is not intended for the party to drink.~

@3055 = ~Brewer's Draught of Enchantment~

@3056 = ~A dark draught kept in an ornate silver-rimmed vessel. The brewer claims it can make the drinker's affections turn toward a chosen beloved. Larissa requested it for her husband. It is not intended for the party to drink.~

@3057 = ~Bassilus~

@3058 = ~Senyan~

@3059 = ~Obsidian Sabre +2~

@3060 = ~Obsidian Sabre +2

This long, dark-hilted sabre is said to have belonged to Fzoul Chembryl, the ruthlessly ambitious priest who held great influence over the religious forces of Zhentil Keep. Fzoul used faith, fear and political cunning as instruments of command. Few who crossed his path ever forgot the price of defiance.

The blade's origins are disputed. Some maintain that Chembryl carried it as a mark of office before setting it aside for more potent symbols of his authority. Its enchantment has endured: the steel burns with a captive spark that scorches whatever it strikes. Whatever its true provenance, the weapon has passed far beyond the hands that once claimed it.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +2 bonus
Damage: 1d8+2 slashing, plus 1 fire damage
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Long Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires: 6 Strength
Weight: 4~

@3061 = ~Hiarfi's Flute~

@3062 = ~Hiarfi's Flute

A carefully crafted wooden flute, presented to Hiarfi upon his graduation from New Olamn, the bards' college in Waterdeep. More than a musical instrument, it is his personal emblem of achievement. Hiarfi's name has been etched discreetly along the lower end.~

@3063 = ~A finely made wooden flute, bearing its owner's name.~

